WEBVTT

00:08:28.938 --> 00:08:31.979
that synthetic happiness
is of an inferior kind.

00:08:32.003 --> 00:08:33.526
Why do we have that belief?

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:35.574
Well, it's very simple.

00:08:35.598 --> 00:08:39.591
What kind of economic engine
would keep churning

00:08:39.615 --> 00:08:42.351
if we believed
that not getting what we want

00:08:42.375 --> 00:08:45.081
could make us just as happy as getting it?

00:08:45.844 --> 00:08:49.061
With all apologies
to my friend Matthieu Ricard,

00:08:49.085 --> 00:08:51.173
a shopping mall full of Zen monks

00:08:51.197 --> 00:08:53.399
is not going to be
particularly profitable,

00:08:53.423 --> 00:08:55.937
because they don't want stuff enough.

00:08:55.961 --> 00:08:57.042
(Laughter)

00:08:57.066 --> 00:08:58.897
I want to suggest to you

00:08:58.921 --> 00:09:02.914
that synthetic happiness
is every bit as real and enduring